---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../design/kit/astro/Hero.astro';
import Ellipse from '../design/kit/astro/Ellipse.astro';
import landscape from '../assets/landscape.jpg';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" description="About the Swiss Minimal design kit.">
  <Hero
    title="About"
    lead="I'm Danny Englander, and I designed Swiss Minimal in collaboration with Claude Code. It pays homage to Swiss design and the grotesque typefaces I love, from Akzidenz-Grotesk to Neue Haas Grotesk, which was renamed Helvetica in 1960."
    image={landscape}
    alt="Wide crop of an abstract composition: a red circle, black and grey shapes and thin black rules"
    caption="A 16:9 crop of the home page artwork, to show the wide hero."
  >
    <p class="lead hero-lead">
      Swiss Minimal is a small design kit for type-led sites: one grotesque typeface, flat color, thick rules and
      almost no decoration, and <a class="link" href="/agents">works well with AI agents</a>.
    </p>
  </Hero>
  <article class="max-w-2xl pb-16 [&>p]:mb-5">
    <p>
      This page exists to check the type scale on running text. Body copy sits at 16px with a line height of
      1.5, which keeps paragraphs open without feeling loose. Headings rely on size and weight alone; there are
      no colored headings, no boxes and no icons to prop them up.
    </p>
    <p>
      The palette is three colors and a vermilion. Cream paper, near-black ink, a muted grey for secondary text,
      and one brand vermilion, a red leaning toward orange, kept for large shapes and the focus ring. Small
      vermilion text uses a darker tone on the page so it still passes contrast.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each page of the menu has its own link. Write to us on the <a class="link" href="#contact">contact page</a>,
      or see the <a class="link" href="#features">features</a> and when each arrived.
    </p>
    <p>
      Code is the one place a second family appears. To start a site,
      copy <code>kit/</code> and <code>fonts/</code> into <code>src/design/</code> and import the kit from your
      global stylesheet; press <kbd>Tab</kbd> to see the focus ring.
    </p>
    <pre class="mb-5" tabindex="0"><code>@import "../design/kit/tailwind.css";
/* site-only CSS below */</code></pre>
    <p>
      Terminal output and logs sit on a dark block, the same in both themes, with commands in bold and
      errors in the accent.
    </p>
    <pre class="pre--bar mb-5" tabindex="0"><code><span class="pre-cmd">$ npm run release -- --dry-run</span>
Tag v2026.10.21, notes from the Features list
<span class="pre-err">Stopped: main is behind origin/main. Pull first.</span></code></pre>
    <p>
      Abbreviations go in an oval badge. Pays homage to international car decals. Allows for 2–4 large block
      letters.
    </p>
    <div class="mb-5 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
      <Ellipse code="CH" label="Switzerland" class="text-5xl" />
      <Ellipse code="CH" label="Switzerland" solid class="text-5xl" />
      <Ellipse code="DE" label="German" class="text-2xl" />
      <Ellipse code="FR" label="French" class="text-2xl" />
      <Ellipse code="NL" label="Netherlands" solid />
      <Ellipse code="USA" label="United States" />
    </div>
    <p class="small muted">
      Set in Overused Grotesk, released under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
    </p>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
